  "content": {
    "title": "ESPN's Jay Bilas picks UCF to advance in March Madness. Here's how far",
    "text": "March 17, 2026, 11:56 a.m. ETESPN analyst Jay Bilas predicts UCF will defeat UCLA in the first round of the 2026 NCAA Tournament.The Knights, a No. 10 seed, are matched against the No. 7 seed Bruins in Philadelphia.He does not expect UCF to advance past the second round, forecasting a loss to UConn.ESPN college basketball analyst Jay Bilas believes Johnny Dawkins, his former teammate at Duke, will lead UCF past the first round of March Madness for the second time.Bilas released his predictions for every game of the 2026 NCAA Tournament to begin the week. The Knights (21-11) drew the No. 10 seed in the East Region and a matchup with UCLA (23-11) at 7:25 p.m. Friday, March 20, at Xfinity Mobile Arena in Philadelphia.Last year, Bilas correctly predicted all four No. 1 seeds would reach the Final Four, and that Florida would battle Houston for the national championship.Stream UCF vs. UCLA live on Sling TV.What Jay Bilas said about UCF vs. UCLA and potentially UConn in NCAA TournamentRegarding the matchup, Bilas said, \"The Bruins have Donovan Dent, one of the five best point guards in the nation, but UCF has Themus Fulks, Jordan Burks and the Big 12's version of Draymond Green in Jamichael Stillwell. With UCLA banged up, the Knights are worth a flier.\"Bilas was on the call for both of UCF's games at the Big 12 tournament last week. The Knights rallied from eight points down to force overtime and later defeat Cincinnati before being ousted in the quarterfinals by eventual champion Arizona.He does not, however, envision the Knights advancing to their first Sweet 16 in Dawkins' hometown of Washington, D.C. Instead, Bilas forecasts second-seed UConn to eliminate the Knights on Sunday.\"I don't have UConn as a Final Four team this year, but the Huskies are a second-weekend team,\" he said.UCF last qualified for the NCAA Tournament in 2019. The Knights knocked off VCU 73-58 behind Tacko Fall's 10 points, 18 rebounds and five blocked shots before falling at the buzzer to top-seeded Duke 77-76.",
